### DamagedProduct Integration Test - Manual HTTP Testing

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@adminToken = <replace with actual admin token>
@productId = <replace with actual product ID>
@shelfId = <replace with actual shelf ID>

### 1. Get Damaged Product Statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/stats

### 2. Get Damaged Products by Product ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/product/{{productId}}

### 3. Get Damaged Product Shelves
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/{{damagedProductId}}/shelves

### 4. Create Damaged Product Report
POST {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "{{productId}}",
  "quantity": 5,
  "damage_reason": "Broken packaging during delivery",
  "reported_date": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "status": "pending"
}

### 5. Create Damaged Product - Expired
POST {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "{{productId}}",
  "quantity": 10,
  "damage_reason": "Expired - Beyond shelf life",
  "reported_date": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "status": "pending"
}

### 6. Create Damaged Product - Water Damage
POST {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "{{productId}}",
  "quantity": 3,
  "damage_reason": "Water damage in warehouse",
  "reported_date": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "status": "pending"
}

### Save Damaged Product ID for Further Tests
@damagedProductId = <replace with actual damaged product ID>

### 7. Adjust Inventory for Damaged Product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/{{damagedProductId}}/adjust-inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity_to_remove": 3,
  "notes": "Removed damaged items from system"
}

### 8. Bulk Update Status - Mark as Resolved
PUT {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/bulk/update-status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ids": ["{{damagedProductId}}"],
  "status": "resolved",
  "resolution_notes": "Items discarded"
}

### 9. Bulk Update Multiple Records
PUT {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/bulk/update-status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ids": [
    "{{damagedProductId1}}",
    "{{damagedProductId2}}",
    "{{damagedProductId3}}"
  ],
  "status": "investigated"
}

### 10. Get All Damaged Products
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products

### 11. Get Damaged Products with Filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products?status=pending

### 12. Get Damaged Products with Date Range
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products?from_date={{$datetime offset(-7, 'd') iso8601}}&to_date={{$datetime iso8601}}

### 13. Update Damage Status Manually
PUT {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/{{damagedProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "resolved",
  "resolution_notes": "Item repaired and restocked"
}

### 14. Get Statistics for Reporting
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/stats?period=month

### 15. Test High Volume Damage Report
POST {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "{{productId}}",
  "quantity": 50,
  "damage_reason": "Bulk damage in transit",
  "reported_date": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "status": "pending",
  "shelf_id": "{{shelfId}}"
}

### 16. Get Shelves with Damaged Items
GET {{baseUrl}}/damaged-products/{{damagedProductId}}/shelves
